title: Edition I Sold Out in Eight Days
---
author: ORGANIZERS
---
pub_date: 2026-10-29
---
body:

Thank you! Edition I of PyCon DE 2027 [went on sale](/blog/pycon-de-2027-is-live/) on 21 October at 12:00 CEST. Today, eight days later, all 150 Early Bird tickets are gone. We're humbled, and a little giddy.

Those 150 people now own a piece of PyCon DE history: the [Edition I shirt](/faqs/#t-shirt-editions), made in exactly the number sold, never to be printed again.

## Edition II is on sale now

[Edition II: Blind Bird](/buy-ticket/) is open. You're buying before the speakers are announced, trusting us to put together a great program in Heidelberg. That trust is rewarded with the second-lowest price of the year:

- **Standard:** 790 €
- **Self-funded:** 500 €
- **Student:** 300 €

Every three-day pass comes with the Edition II shirt, again made only in the number sold. Choose your [T-shirt size](/blog/t-shirt-sizes/) with care.

## Don't wait for Edition III

Edition II runs until **10 February 2027**. That's the day we announce the talks accepted through our [Call for Proposals](/call-for-proposals/) and switch to Edition III: Wise Bird, at a higher price. Once an edition closes, it never reopens. And our promise holds: no ticket will ever be sold cheaper than the one before it. No promo codes, no last-minute deals.

## Training budget left for 2026?

If your team still has education budget left for this year, now is the moment. Book your PyCon DE 2027 ticket, or a [masterclass](/masterclasses/), before the year ends, and the invoice is dated 2026. Three days of talks, a day of hands-on training and the [sprints](/sprints/): it's hard to find a better use for what's left in the budget.

If the ticket price stands between you and PyCon DE, apply to our [Financial Aid Programme](/financial-aid/) by 27 December.

[Get your Edition II ticket](/buy-ticket/)

See you in Heidelberg.

— The PyCon DE Team
---
